From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 20:15:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] GBM: present the GUI plane on the display clock

Games tear; the GUI and video do not.

The GBM backend takes the DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_NONBLOCK path whenever it is not
drawing to the video plane, so a commit returns before the flip and the next
frame can land part way down the screen. Video never showed it because video
goes out on the video plane, where async is already false. Games render to the
GUI plane.

It only became visible once a game had the headroom to outrun the panel: the
Saturn on yabause renders 60.5fps against 59.94Hz and tears, while the same
game on beetle-saturn - too slow to reach 60 - does not, because being late is
its own throttle. Kodi's own vsync setting cannot help, SetVSyncImpl on this
backend is an empty stub.

A blocking commit waits for the flip, which is what vsync means here. The GUI
is drawn well inside a frame either way, so it gives up nothing for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -144,7 +144,17 @@
 
   if (rendered || videoLayer)
   {
-    bool async = !videoLayer && m_eglFence;
+    // Present the GUI plane on the display's clock, not as fast as it can.
+    //
+    // async takes the DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_NONBLOCK path, so the commit returns
+    // before the flip and the next frame can land mid-scanout. Video never
+    // noticed, because it goes out on the video plane where async is already
+    // false; games render to the GUI plane and do notice. A Saturn core with
+    // headroom ran at 60.5fps against a 59.94Hz panel and tore, while the same
+    // game on a core too slow to reach 60 did not - being late is its own
+    // throttle. A blocking commit waits for the flip, which is what vsync means
+    // here, and the GUI is drawn well inside a frame either way.
+    bool async = false;
     if (rendered)
     {
 #if defined(EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync) && defined(EGL_KHR_fence_sync)
